  "problem": "| $x$ | $-8$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $-2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ |\n\nLet ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{65}$ be a random sample of size $n=65$ from a population with the probability mass function given above. Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is less than $-4.9.$\n\n*Note: $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*",
